        "text_3DhUyN": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "content_alignment": "left",
            "subheading": "",
            "heading": "What are Some Key Safety Applications for Adhesive Tapes?",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2",
            "description": "<p>The wide range of safety tape designs makes them useful for applications across a wide range of industries. Industrial applications incorporate safety tapes for product and equipment identification, color coding, flagging, product bundling, and as aisle markings. Barricade tapes are often used during emergencies to prevent unwanted intrusion in sensitive or dangerous areas. Adhesive tapes get used on walls, floors, stairs, equipment, and other locations in public and commercial buildings to provide direction and ensure the safety of employees and visitors.</p><p>Safety tapes can support safety measures in a variety of settings, including:</p><ul><li>Schools</li><li>Warehouses</li><li>Industrial facilities</li><li>Corporate offices</li><li>Hospitals</li><li>Construction sites</li></ul>",
            "text_size": "text-base",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "btn--primary",
            "button_icon": "none",
            "width": "50%",
